f cards and take control?"\n\n**The Problem - Limited Options:** I see the "Valid Moves" list the user gave me, and it doesn\'t include "airplane with wings" - which is my ideal play. Now, I have to think, how do I play this hand to get out of this jam with this low singles?\n\n**Initial Strategy:** I have to utilize those strong triples. So the move here is a little bit more conservative, but it keeps my cards in control to force the hands from my opponent. The play is `♣3 ♠Q ♥Q ♦Q`.\nThe plan is to leverage the Queens. This play clears one of the problem low cards (the 3) and forces someone to play over that. In other words, to put the pressure on my opponent. I will still get my strong cards back.\n\n**The Bigger Picture:** This play will force other players to break their triple sequences or use high value cards (2s or Aces). If they play 2, I can come back with a powerful play and take the initiative.\n\n**Why Not Other Options?** If I begin with a small single, this will leave me with a bunch of random cards and I might have to use my Rocket. In the beginning, this is not optimal. So, in the end, I need to find a way to make sure the hand is a good fit.\n\n**Final Decision:** Given the limitations, the best move is to play `♣3 ♠Q ♥Q ♦Q`. It’s not the most aggressive, but it\'s strategic, forces other players to act, and sets me up for a better position later.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The Landlord holds a strong hand with a Rocket (Double Joker), two triples (QQQ, KKK), and top pairs (AA), but suffers from several disconnected low singles (3, 4, 5, 6, 9, J). The "Valid Moves" list indicates that playing an Airplane with attached singles (QQQKKK+34) is not currently available/valid, only the bare Airplane or individual Triples with attachments. Playing the bare Airplane is inefficient as it leaves the low singles stranded. Playing a single 3 is weak against opponents holding four 2s.\n\nThe optimal strategy is to split the Airplane into two "Triple with Single" plays. Playing `triple_with_single: ♣3 ♠Q ♥Q ♦Q` allows you to discard the lowest junk card (3). Since you hold AA, opponents cannot beat QQQ with AAA; they must use a Triple of 2s or a Bomb. If they spend 222, your remaining KKK becomes dominant. You retain the Rocket and AA for control.\n\nReason: This move maximizes card efficiency by carrying a junk card (3) with a strong triple (QQQ). It leverages the ownership of AA to force out the opponents\' highest cards (222) or Bombs, while keeping the Rocket and KKK for subsequent plays.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣3", "♠Q", "♥Q", "♦Q"]}'}
